# Normalize line endings - store LF in the repository, check out native.
* text=auto
# BEGIN launcher-line-endings - generated, do not edit here
# These lines are the environment's, and they are here because the launchers are. A launcher is
# generated into this project by `Commands/materialize-projects.py`, and git decides on checkout what
# line endings it gets. Without these rules `text=auto` hands a `.sh` CRLF on Windows, where it fails
# with "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M" - a message that names neither the file nor the problem - and
# hands a `.bat` LF, which cmd.exe misreads in ways that look like a corrupt script.
#
# Measured 2026-08-28: sixteen of eighteen projects had no such rule, and the launchers had already
# split into one text in two line endings because of it.
#
# Everything outside this region is the project's own. Add what this project needs beside it.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
*.zsh   text eol=lf
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
# END launcher-line-endings

# The web sources are served as they are stored. Keep them LF so a diff shows the change
# and not the line endings.
*.html  text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.webmanifest text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

# Binary - never touch these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff2 binary
